====================================
  UPDATES 2006: quick summary
====================================

* TRACEMIN added (also in input decks, with options)
  Please, read the README file in TRACEMIN before attempting to use it. 
  ./TRACEMIN/README

* The input decks have been updated: list of new parameters can be found in 
  ./nemo3d/example/README_Updates_May06. 
  Shall you have an old input deck (Version = 0.17), you'll need to 
  update it to Version 0.18, using the script "update-nemo3d-input.pl", 
  which can be found in ~/My_path_to_NEMO_3D/NEMO_3D/nemo3d/misc/: 

  > (PATH_TO_UPDATES)/update-nemo3d-input.pl my_input_deck.xml

  where eg. (PATH_TO_UPDATES) = ~/My_path_to_NEMO_3D/NEMO_3D/nemo3d/misc/   
  Then, you'll get as an output, your file 'my_input_deck.xm" OVERWRITTEN:
  take this into account, if you want to re-use it!

* New options in build's make: by typing

  > make test 

  four test will be run in will run a test and compare 
  output files with old ones: 
  Howto:
  -----
  1. Change to the NEMO_3D/build/ directory,
     > cd ~/My_path_to_NEMO_3D/NEMO_3D/build/

  2. Make the test, just type
     > make test

  Output:
  -------
  The tests can take about 15mins to be finished.

  OK: If everything is OK, then the eigenvaules in
     NEMO_3D/nemo3d/example/TestRun/inputs/*.nd_Ek_ascii
     will be the same as the old ones,
     NEMO_3D/nemo3d/example/TestRun/*.old_nd_Ek.
     One gets in the output:

       ===== NEMO_3D TEST MADE: CONGRATULLATIONS! test OK ====

  NOT OK: If the executable is producing a different output,
     you will see in the output a warning message:

       ===== NEMO_3D TEST MADE:  WARNING: Your new executable is
       producing DIFFERENT OUTPUT than before!!! =====
    
     -Check differences between old and new eigenvalues in
      NEMO_3D/nemo3d/example/TestRun/*.difs
     -Check the output from NEMO_3D: that is dumped in *.out

* Bug: in ./PostNEMO3D/Makefile the variable LDOPT has been updated: as a 
  result, postprocess runs also in LEAR cluster now... 

